    cogn: "The People's Republic was proclaimed on 31 December 1969; the previous name was restored in 1991 (Sovereign National Conference).",
    gab: "There was a French presence in Libreville from 1839–1849; Gabon was part of French Congo and a separate colony from 1904.",
    dji: "France bought Obock in 1862 but did not set up an administration there until 1884.",
    ken: "The Imperial British East Africa Company (1888) preceded the protectorate of 1895. Rudolf Province (Turkana) was part of Uganda until 1926, and Jubaland part of Kenya until 1925.",
    tza: "The German East Africa Company received its imperial charter in 1885; resistance (Abushiri, 1888–89; Mkwawa and the Hehe, 1891–98) delayed the conquest. Zanzibar and Pemba were a British protectorate (1890–1963) and joined Tanganyika in 1964.",
    tza1919: "British and Belgian troops occupied the colony in 1916–1917; the British mandate of Tanganyika was formalised in 1920–1922.",
    tgo: "French and British troops occupied Togo in August 1914 and divided it between them (mandates of 1922). British Togoland was integrated into Ghana in 1956–57.",
    cmr: "Between 1911 and 1916 Kamerun included Neukamerun, ceded by France (parts of present-day Gabon, Congo, the Central African Republic and Chad). The Allies occupied it between 1914 and 1916. Southern British Cameroons joined Cameroon in 1961; the northern part joined Nigeria.",
    nam: "Walvis Bay was British (1878), passed to South Africa and was not returned to Namibia until 1994. In 1971 the International Court of Justice declared the South African occupation illegal.",
    swz: "By the convention of 1894 Swaziland came under the protection of the South African Republic (Transvaal); after the Anglo-Boer War it passed to British administration (1903).",
    zmb: "The British South Africa Company (BSAC) extended its administration north of the Zambezi from 1890–1891 (treaty with Lewanika, the Lozi king, 1890). Northern Rhodesia was formed in 1911 and passed to the Crown in 1924.",
