    eth: "During the partition, Ethiopia itself expanded militarily to the south, east and west (Harar, 1887; Oromo, Sidama, Wolaita and Somali territories, between 1880 and 1900), with great violence. Its present borders come from this expansion and from treaties with the European powers. Source: Bahru Zewde, <i>A History of Modern Ethiopia 1855–1991</i> (2001).",
