    // Events
    berlin: "Participants: Austria-Hungary, Belgium, Denmark, France, Germany, Italy, the Netherlands, the Ottoman Empire, Portugal, Russia, Spain, Sweden-Norway, the United Kingdom and the United States. Source: S. Förster, W. J. Mommsen and R. Robinson (eds.), <i>Bismarck, Europe and Africa: The Berlin Africa Conference 1884–1885</i> (1988).",
    congo: "The death toll is debated because there are no reliable censuses. A. Hochschild, <i>King Leopold's Ghost</i> (1998), following J. Vansina, estimates a population loss of about 10 million people between 1880 and 1920; other historians give lower figures. Causes include killings, famine, disease and a falling birth rate.",
